course: dictionary
lesson: 4781
title: Hug: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «Oisin hugged him» means he put his arms around him and held him close, because the words around hug tell you it is about people.
explain: Hug can also be a noun, «a hug», which is the warm action itself. In «Mum hugs him», after Fergus wins a silver medal, the hug shows she is proud of him, even though Dad teases him afterwards and it hurts.
explain: Some hugs are not yours to give or take. You can say no to a hug, and you should always ask before you hug someone else. Knowing that your body is your own is an important lesson.
explain: Hug can also mean to stay very close to something. «The path hugs the coast» means the path runs right along the edge of the sea. To check your meaning, swap in a phrase like stays very close to and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Hug means to put your arms around someone and hold them close, to show love, comfort or friendship.
fact: A hug is the action itself, and hugs is its plural: «a big hug», «a group hug».
fact: A hug can comfort someone who is sad, and in stories it often shows that love has come back after an argument.
fact: You can say no to a hug, and you should ask before you hug others.
fact: «The path hugs the coast» means the path stays very close to the coast.
exercise: «Oisin hugged him» — what does hugged mean here? | Hid behind him | Ran past him very fast | Pushed him hard away | *Put his arms around him and held him close
exercise: «The path hugs the coast.» What does hugs mean here? | Runs far away from | Jumps over | *Stays very close to | Is covered by
exercise: What should you do before you hug someone else? | Run away | Give them a present | Shout across the room | *Ask first
test: «Mum was upset, then hugged him and said "thank you for telling me".» What does the hug show? | Mum is lost | Mum is angry and will shout | *Mum is comforting him and is glad he told the truth | Mum is hungry
test: «Esau ran to meet Jacob and hugged him instead of taking revenge.» What does this hug show? | Tiredness | Fear of the dark | Anger and a wish to fight | *Forgiveness, not anger
exam: Which sentence uses hug as a noun? | They are hugging on the sofa | The path hugs the coast | *Mum gave him a big hug | Oisin hugged his dad
